{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1e6f2a0-4c2e-4a3a-9b0d-socialmedia-api",
    "name": "Social Media REST API",
    "description": "Complete API collection for the Social Media platform (Spring Boot 3.3.0 / Java 21, package `com.shishir.socialmedia`).\n\nCovers all seven implemented features: Authentication (register/login/JWT), Users, Posts, Comments, Likes, Follow, Feed & Timeline, and Search.\n\n## Auth model\nThe collection uses collection-level Bearer auth backed by the `{{jwt_token}}` variable, so every request inherits it automatically. Endpoints that are `permitAll()` in `SecurityConfig` (public GETs, register, login) explicitly override auth to \"No Auth\" so they work with an empty token too.\n\n## Quick start\n1. Import this collection and the `socialmedia-api-environment.json` environment, then select it (top-right dropdown).\n2. Run **Authentication > Register User**, then **Authentication > Login User** — its Tests script automatically saves `jwt_token`, `user_id`, and `username` into the active environment.\n3. Run **Posts > Create Post** — saves `post_id`. Run **Comments > Create Comment** — saves `comment_id`.\n4. Everything else now works out of the box.\n\n## Switching environments\nImport `socialmedia-api-environment.json` (local dev, `http://localhost:8080`) or `socialmedia-api-production.json` (prod placeholder URL) and swap between them from the environment dropdown — every request uses `{{base_url}}`, so nothing else needs to change.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{jwt_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level pre-request script.",
          "// Runs before every request; currently a no-op hook kept for future shared setup",
          "// (e.g. auto-refreshing an expiring token) without needing to touch every request."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level test script, runs after every request's own Tests script.",
          "pm.test('Response time is acceptable (< 5000ms)', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(5000);",
          "});",
          "",
          "pm.test('Response has JSON content-type (when body present)', function () {",
          "    if (pm.response.code !== 204 && pm.response.body && pm.response.body.length) {",
          "        pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json');",
          "    }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "description": "Register, login, and fetch the authenticated user's own profile from a JWT (`AuthController`).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register User",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{test_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{test_password}}\",\n  \"username\": \"{{test_username}}\",\n  \"firstName\": \"John\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Doe\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Create a new user account. Validation: email must be valid, password min 8 chars, username 3-50 chars.\n\n**Responses:** 201 Created, 400 validation failed, 409 email/username already exists."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has user profile fields', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('id');",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('username');",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('email');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('user_id', json.id);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('username', json.username);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login User",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{test_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{test_password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticate with email/password and receive a JWT.\n\n**Responses:** 200 OK with `LoginResponse` (token, type, userId, username, email, expiresIn), 401 invalid password, 404 no account with this email."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains a JWT token', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json).to.have.property('token');",
                  "    pm.expect(json.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set('jwt_token', json.token);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('user_id', json.userId);",
                  "    pm.environment.set('username', json.username);",
                  "    console.log('Saved jwt_token, user_id, username to environment');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Current User",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Get the authenticated user's own profile, resolved from the JWT.\n\n**Auth required.** Responses: 200 OK, 401 missing/invalid token."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Returned profile matches logged-in user', function () {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(String(json.id)).to.eql(String(pm.environment.get('user_id')));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
